cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AM-Bench in your research, please cite the paper below."
title: "AM-Bench: A Modular Simulation Suite and Benchmark for Aerial Manipulation Policy Learning"
abstract: >-
  AM-Bench is a modular simulation suite and benchmark for aerial manipulation
  policy learning, built on Isaac Lab. It provides representative embodiments
  spanning underactuated, fully actuated, and overactuated systems, 12 tasks
  across contact, transport, and constrained interaction, configurable
  aerodynamic disturbances and actuator saturation, standard low-level
  controllers, and baseline policy-learning algorithms.
